e traces campus welcoming efforts to 1955 and says Welcome Week, formerly called Passages, now helps new and returning students acclimate through tours and events.","source_url":"https://traditions.illinoisstate.edu/traditions/welcome-week/","source_title":"Welcome Week | Traditions | Illinois State","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Welcome Week takes place around the start of the academic year; individual programs may be limited to students or require registration.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"isu-alma-mater-harmony","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Illinois State Alma Mater","title":"A School Hymn Distilled into Four-Part Harmony","subtitle":"The Redbird alma mater performed from a hymn composed during 1913–14","notes":"Listen to the Big Red Marching Machine’s four-part arrangement before an event, then follow the printed words when the campus sings together.","short_summary":"Illinois State’s alma mater preserves a compact portion of an older school hymn.","evidence_claim":"Illinois State says its Alma Mater is a shortened version of the school hymn composed by Gussie Schneider during the 1913–14 school year and documents a four-part band performance.","source_url":"https://traditions.illinoisstate.edu/traditions/alma-mater/","source_title":"Alma Mater | Traditions | Illinois State","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The tradition appears at university performances and ceremonies; access depends on the host event’s admission rules.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"isu-gamma-phi-circus","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Gamma Phi Circus","title":"A College Circus That Is Greek by Name Only","subtitle":"Illinois State’s student circus tradition, organized in 1926","notes":"Watch for tumbling, aerial, balance, and ensemble acts at the annual show; use official performance guidance for any audience participation.","short_summary":"Redbird performers sustain a collegiate circus tradition with roots in campus athletics.","evidence_claim":"Illinois State says Gamma Phi Circus dates to 1926, is not part of the Greek system, and is the oldest collegiate circus in the United States.","source_url":"https://traditions.illinoisstate.edu/traditions/gamma-phi/","source_title":"Gamma Phi Circus | Traditions | Illinois State","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Annual performances are traditionally staged in April; current dates, venue rules, and ticket requirements should be checked with Gamma Phi Circus.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"isu-wear-red-friday","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Wear Red on Friday","title":"Friday Has an Official Color","subtitle":"The weekly Redbird custom introduced by a campus-community pride committee","notes":"Add a red layer or existing Redbird item on Friday; participation is the color cue itself, so no special purchase is necessary.","short_summary":"Students, employees, alumni, and friends use Friday clothing as a recurring campus signal.","evidence_claim":"Illinois State documents a Friday tradition in which students, faculty, staff, alumni, and friends wear red or Redbird gear; the idea began in the early 2000s.","source_url":"https://traditions.illinoisstate.edu/traditions/red/","source_title":"Wear Red on Friday | Traditions | Illinois State","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This weekly tradition can be observed anywhere on campus or in the community; specific events m